# Dependency Injection

## Purpose

One composition root, predictable lifetimes, no codegen surprises.

## When Applied

Adding or wiring services, repositories, datasources, BLoCs, or Cubits.

## Requirements

- Library: GetIt (`final sl = GetIt.I`). Composition root: `lib/core/di/injection.dart` → `setupDI()`.
- Lifetimes: `SupabaseClient`, repositories, datasources, cache, tab controllers, `UserQrService` = **lazy singleton**; BLoCs/Cubits = **factory**; `AdminSessionPreferences` = eager singleton (async create).
- Manual registration only — no `injectable`/codegen.
- Prefer constructor injection into BLoCs/Cubits; wire `BlocProvider` at the page boundary with `sl<MyBloc>()`.

## Examples

```dart
sl.registerLazySingleton<CoachRepository>(() => CoachRepository(sl()));
sl.registerFactory<BookingBloc>(() => BookingBloc(sl()));
```

## Anti-patterns

- Constructing a repository directly inside a widget or page.
- Registering a BLoC/Cubit as a singleton (stale state across screens).

## Common Mistakes

- Forgetting to register a new type, then hitting a runtime `GetIt` error.
- Adding `injectable` annotations expecting codegen to run.
